.git
.gitignore

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/

# Virtual environments
.venv/

# Test / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage/

# Local development. The `**/` prefix is load-bearing: a .dockerignore entry with
# no slash matches the context ROOT only, so a bare `.env` leaves `migrations/.env`
# and `vektra-*/src/.env` in the build context, and the Dockerfile copies those
# directories whole. Measured against a real docker build (INFRA-008): with `.env`,
# both `sub/.env` and `sub/deep/.env` were copied into the image; with `**/.env`
# none was, and unrelated nested files still arrived. The image is published to a
# public registry on every tag, so a file that reaches it is world-readable.
# `.env.example` is excluded too: nothing copies it into the image, and a COPY that
# needed it would fail loudly rather than ship a secret quietly.
# vektra-shared/tests/test_image_content_boundary.py fails if these rules regress.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/CLAUDE.local.md
**/.claude/
**/.local/
# Assess keyrings (`make assess-keys` writes ./secrets/assess/, gitignored): mounted as
# Compose secrets at run time, never baked into the image, at the root or nested.
**/secrets/
# VEKTRA_ASSESS_SECRETS_PATH may point the keyrings at any directory, including one the
# Dockerfile copies (e.g. ./migrations/private), so the fixed file names are excluded too,
# wherever they are. The list is docker-compose.assess.yml's `secrets:` file names;
# test_image_content_boundary.py fails if one is missing here.
**/assess_db_api_password
**/assess_db_worker_password
**/assess_handoff_private
**/assess_handoff_public
**/assess_kek
**/assess_smtp
**/assess_teacher_config_private
**/assess_teacher_config_public
**/assess_token_signing
**/assess_transcript_kek
**/assess_ws_tokens

# S2S planning artifacts
.s2s/

# Documentation and CI (not needed in image)
.github/
docs/
*.md
!vektra-*/README.md
# Defensive: keep alembic.ini in context if a future *.ini glob is added
!alembic.ini

# Archive
.archive/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The assess discussion UI (plan 9): dependencies and any locally built bundle stay out; the
# image gets the bundle from the assess-ui-builder stage only
**/node_modules
vektra-assess/src/vektra_assess/ui/static
